Tonnes to grams takes two steps to smaller units. Multiply by $1000$ at each step.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\node (t) at (0,0) {$0.0062\,\mathrm{t}$};
\node (kg) at (42,0) {$6.2\,\mathrm{kg}$};
\node (g) at (84,0) {$6200\,\mathrm{g}$};
\draw[->] (t) -- node[above] {$\times1000$} (kg);
\draw[->] (kg) -- node[above] {$\times1000$} (g);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}0.0062\times1000\times1000\\&=6.2\times1000\\&=6200\end{aligned}$

$0.0062\text{ t}=6200\text{ g}$.
